  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Scaling-up of high impact interventions in the fight against TB based on the STOP TB strategy - Burkina Faso (01-Jul-2015-31-Dec-2017)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Burkina Faso, Tuberculosis, Programme d&apos;Appui au D&#xe9;veloppement Sanitaire (PADS) (PADS)This program has the following goals: Reduce TB prevalence from 80 cases per 100,000 population in 2013 to 72 cases per 100,000 population in Burkina Faso by the end 2017. The objectives of this program are: Decrease TB/HIV co-infection related deaths from 19.6% (2013 cohort) to less than 5% by the end of 2017 (2016 cohort).  Improve program management and strategic information availability.  Increase treatment success rate of MDR-TB cases from 57.7% (2012 cohort) to at least 75% by end of 2017 (2016 cohort).  Increase treatment success rate of TB cases in all forms from 79.8% (2013 cohort) to at least 90% by end of 2017 (2016 cohort)</narrative>
  </description>
